.TH DWGPLOT "1" "November 2026" "dwgplot 0.15" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dwgplot \- manual page for dwgplot 0.15
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dwgplot
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... \fI\,DWGFILE >PLOTFILE\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Converts some 2D elements of the DWG to a format of GNU plotutils.
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-output\-format\fR FMT
One of: png, pnm, gif (bitmaps), or
svg, ps, ai, cgm, fig, pcl, hpgl,
regis, tek (vector formats).
The default is meta, the plot(5)
format for plot(1) or graph(1).
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR FILE
output file, else stdout
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-pagesize\fR SIZE
e.g. a4, letter, or a4,xsize=10in
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-bitmapsize\fR WxH
of png, pnm and gif. default 1024x1024
.TP
\fB\-v[0\-9]\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR [0\-9]
verbosity
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-mspace\fR
only model\-space, no paper\-space
.TP
\fB\-\-force\-free\fR
force free
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
display this help and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
output version information and exit
.PP
GNU LibreDWG online manual: <https://www.gnu.org/software/libredwg/>
.SH "SEE ALSO"
